                <pb facs="0433" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/29370: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-09T12:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 10—1:08
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>319.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The Minister of Finance, Montes de Oca, has requested that Mr. Morrow be informed
                    that political events of the past week have rendered it desirable to leave debt
                    negotiations and plans for railroad reorganization <hi rendition="#italic">in
                        statu quo</hi> until the situation becomes somewhat clarified, which might
                    be within a few days or a few weeks. The Minister of Finance does not know, as
                    yet, just what effect General Calles’ change in political plans may have on his
                    position in regard to railroad reorganization.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
